Bug_Details:
Both branches contain identical code Branching constructs (if statements, conditional expressions) should contain
difference code in the two branches. Repeating identical code in both branches
is usually a bug. For example: condition ? same : same condition ? same : same if (condition) {
  same();
} else {
  same();
} if (condition) {
  same();
} else {
  same();
} this usually indicates a typo where one of the branches was supposed to contain
different logic: condition ? something : somethingElse condition ? something : somethingElse if (condition) {
  doSomething();
} else {
  doSomethingElse();
} if (condition) {
  doSomething();
} else {
  doSomethingElse();
}
